{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-009", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: diagnostics of the PULL_UP decline with exposure. With lineup fixed effects the slope was -0.0255; without them -0.0063, and the same-shooter placebo on other play types was -0.0071 to -0.0075, consistent with a shooter-level confound. Applies to exposure-effect claims for one play type that lack a same-shooter placebo. The verdict is the extractor's reading of diagnostics; there is no written conclusion.", "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-009 | Study family SF-TMP-009: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- observed_research_question: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The PULL_UP-specific decline with exposure is defensive adaptation rather than shooter selection/lineup artifact.\n- observed_result: With lineup FE: slope holding shot fixed -0.0255 (0.0061); shooter's earlier scored -0.1044 vs not scored +0.0693. No lineup FE: -0.0063 (0.0036); placebo other play types -0.0075 (0.0017).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Effect shrinks from -0.0255 to -0.0063 without lineup FE and the same-shooter placebo on other play types is -0.0071/-0.0075, consistent with shooter-level confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-012", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: audited the published suppression excess against five null-model families. A within-unit permutation null reproduces it (0.3798 vs 0.3744, z 0.40), so the excess is mechanical under the selection rule; drift-centering removes the tail asymmetry. Applies to estimates that select units on a large drop and compare them with matched controls.", "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-012 | Study family SF-TMP-012: Tail/null-model audit of the published suppression excess\n- observed_research_question: Tail/null-model audit of the published suppression excess\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The published suppression excess (trigger drop minus matched control drop) exceeds appropriate null models and is asymmetric between decline and improvement tails.\n- observed_result: Reproduced excess 0.4080 CI [0.378,0.438]; G within-unit perm at 0.25: obs 0.3798 null 0.3744 resid +0.0054 z 0.40; asym neg-pos 0.0176 p 0.258; drift-centered tail mass ratio 1.007.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:drift\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:insufficient_exposure\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-TMP-001"}, {"id": "FAM:SF09", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: two records on opponent POST_UP then PUTBACK stacking before a star possession. Stacked suppression (-0.071, n=1,047) was smaller than either alone and far below the additive prediction (-0.232); one cluster gradient had an unexpected sign and per-player stacked n was often under 5. Applies to additive-stacking claims and per-player stacked estimates.", "document": "# FAM:SF09 | Study family SF09: Double-suppression stacking (POST_UP then PUTBACK)\n- observed_research_question: Double-suppression stacking (POST_UP then PUTBACK)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Opponent POST_UP then PUTBACK stacks additively against the next star possession.\n- observed_result: [APPA-057] Baseline 1.210 n=960,764. After PUTBACK only 1.097 d=-0.113 n=15,898. After POST_UP only 1.091 d=-0.119 n=76,329. Stacked 1.138 d=-0.071 n=1,047 vs additive prediction -0.232. Mitchell after PUTBACK 0.919 vs 1 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [APPS-042] POST_UP Q1->Q4 -0.065 (Q1 -0.119 to Q4 -0.184); PUTBACK -0.374 (0.144 to -0.23). TRANSITION cluster gradient +0.075 (unexpected vs hypothesized flat). Stacked delta -0.071 vs additive prediction -0.232 (less t [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: none (no failure recorded)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:implementation_bug\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:IMPLEMENTATION_BUG"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-021", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: pilot test of behavior change when the defense enters the penalty (3 to 4 team fouls), on possessions with clock over 2:30 and game x offense x period fixed effects. The penalty contrast was not distinct from the 2-to-3 and 4-to-5+ placebo contrasts, and standard errors were not printed. Applies to penalty-state effects judged against adjacent-foul placebos.", "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-021 | Study family SF-TMP-021: Penalty-state adaptation (Pilot A)\n- observed_research_question: Penalty-state adaptation (Pilot A)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Behavior changes when the defense enters the penalty (3->4 team fouls).\n- observed_result: any_fta 3->4 -0.151 vs placebos -5.556/-9.655; rim_pct +0.015 vs +1.666/+2.077; pts +0.020.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Penalty contrast not distinct from placebo contrasts; SEs not printed (sqrt warning).\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: TMP-021: 'with clock>2:30, game x offense x period fe; 2->3 and 4->5+ placebos. any_fta 3->4 -0.151 vs placebos -5.556/-9.655; rim_pct +0'\n- observed_method: Possessions with clock>2:30, game x offense x period FE; 2->3 and 4->5+ placebos.\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear"}], "n_results": 4}

